2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186263467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265346 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "37f3949b-96c0-5579-a5af-c7efac7bcd67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266018 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266018 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266018 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266018 #edb/ref 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266018 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7dfd4e6-f98f-5d70-9672-fbeae076cac0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266018 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $2$ pivots in the $2$nd and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275790 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275790 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275790 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23104f3a-32df-5eb8-b625-6064a0927bc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276109 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 175921860