in{aligned}k(x+1),\\, & 2<x<3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278186 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c628a4a3-1d03-5b7a-9d8c-d548c59d8196" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278186 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nFor the given function, the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}k(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}k(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =k{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =k([\\frac{9}{2}+3]-[\\frac{4}{2}+2]) \\\\  & =k(\\frac{9}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{2}k=1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305785 #edb/ref 1080 "y=-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x+\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305785 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305785 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4099c08f-db10-5b94-b476-722ec92e2f91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305805 #edb/ref 1080 "y=-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305805 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305805 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "424f3742-f4f4-58bf-9771-5a09636ce05b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306503 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306503 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306503 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8ea666d9-fb1e-528b-9c1a-2a72695635a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306732 #edb/ref 1080 "y=-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306732 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306732 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a7e7baf